    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d774">

                <pb facs="0885" n="1719" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/11163</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Willard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Sebastian</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-29T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 29, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 30, 1.55
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1743. Late yesterday afternoon Prime Minister summoned all Ministers, diplomats
                    absent to come to Madrid immediately for council to be held there today. They
                    declined to give any information as to reason for this sudden meeting. Embassy
                    has just learned that Spanish ship <hi rendition="#italic">Carasa</hi> which
                    left Bilbao for Cardiff with cargo of minerals on August 19, has been torpedoed.
                    Six victims, no further details known at present. News of first sinking
                    doubtless known to Spanish Government yesterday and was reason for council. In
                    view of recent Spanish note to Germany (1708, August 22, 2 p.m., and 1725,
                    August 29 [<hi rendition="#italic">25</hi>], 10 a.m.), a very grave situation
                    has arisen.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Willard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
